{"schemaVersion":2,"dialogueId":"Dlg_3415A3FA","title":"Band Member 2 - The Singer","entry":"Dlg_3415A3FA::entry","exit":"Dlg_3415A3FA::exit","nodes":[{"id":"DFr_ECAB63DD","articyId":"72057752951739426","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"Can I help?","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Can I help?","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":425.0,"y":75.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"44574","byteOffset":31193072,"byteLength":320}},{"id":"DFr_9EF11297","articyId":"72057752951739440","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"Fauxter’s still chasing nostalgia, huh? Look, kid, that band had its time. We played our hearts out, burned bright, and burned out. I’m not interested in reliving the past.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Fauxter’s still chasing nostalgia, huh? Look, kid, that band had its time. We played our hearts out, burned bright, and burned out. I’m not interested in reliving the past.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":1050.0,"y":75.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"26948","byteOffset":18075160,"byteLength":556}},{"id":"DFr_D9FDC879","articyId":"72057752951739468","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"That’s sweet, but sentiment doesn’t change the past. Some things don’t come back, no matter how much you want them to.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"That’s sweet, but sentiment doesn’t change the past. Some things don’t come back, no matter how much you want them to.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":1675.0,"y":-175.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"51753","byteOffset":33995536,"byteLength":432}},{"id":"DFr_E3A230E8","articyId":"72057752951739474","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"A legend? That’s just a fancy way of saying I got old. The music never leaves you, but the stage… that’s a different story.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"A legend? That’s just a fancy way of saying I got old. The music never leaves you, but the stage… that’s a different story.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":1675.0,"y":75.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"42955","byteOffset":30580760,"byteLength":440}},{"id":"DFr_2CB85B20","articyId":"72057752951739480","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"…New, huh? No forced reunion, no ghosts of what we used to be? Just music?","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"…New, huh? No forced reunion, no ghosts of what we used to be? Just music?","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":1675.0,"y":325.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"25806","byteOffset":17645672,"byteLength":384}},{"id":"DFr_669390A6","articyId":"72057752951739498","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"That’s a dangerous offer to make a singer, kid. But you know what? I’ll bite. If Fauxter’s serious, tell him I’ll lend my voice. Something new. Not a revival—just… a beginning.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"That’s a dangerous offer to make a singer, kid. But you know what? I’ll bite. If Fauxter’s serious, tell him I’ll lend my voice. Something new. Not a revival—just… a beginning.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":2275.0,"y":325.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"32228","byteOffset":20072336,"byteLength":496}},{"id":"DFr_41177C89","articyId":"72057752951739512","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"Yeah? Well, I’ll believe that when I see him sober enough to say it himself.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Yeah? Well, I’ll believe that when I see him sober enough to say it himself.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":2875.0,"y":325.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"39241","byteOffset":29177288,"byteLength":420}},{"id":"DFr_17AC754E","articyId":"72057821671324296","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"Hi.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Hi.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":-1075.0,"y":325.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"21315","byteOffset":15950600,"byteLength":348}},{"id":"DFr_4F85A82C","articyId":"72057821671324310","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"Judge said the real punishment for me was to remain free, unable to perform Jazz.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Judge said the real punishment for me was to remain free, unable to perform Jazz.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":-475.0,"y":325.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"26242","byteOffset":17809088,"byteLength":392}},{"id":"DFr_A263114F","articyId":"72057821671324317","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"Or I could go to Luna and croon for rich CEO's. Uh...","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Or I could go to Luna and croon for rich CEO's. Uh...","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":-175.0,"y":325.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"45695","byteOffset":31618760,"byteLength":400}},{"id":"DFr_24F1D188","articyId":"72057821671324338","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"I will never croon.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"I will never croon.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":2,"name":"Upset"},"position":{"x":425.0,"y":325.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"19506","byteOffset":15264432,"byteLength":328}},{"id":"DFr_E7300B39","articyId":"72057821671324347","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"Hi.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Hi.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":{"value":0,"name":"Unspecified"},"position":{"x":-175.0,"y":950.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"32067","byteOffset":20012432,"byteLength":312}},{"id":"DFr_D5E3D172","articyId":"72057821671324369","type":"line","className":"DemeanorTemplate","speaker":"Andrea Cellini","text":"I've tried to sing in other genres, but my heart just doesn't beat to disco or pop or opera. Or... sea shanties.","speakerId":"Ntt_A5F46049","textSo